  ],
  "lead": "\"Birthday\" is a song by American singer Katy Perry from her fourth studio album, Prism (2013). She co-wrote the song with Bonnie McKee and its producers Dr. Luke, Max Martin, and Cirkut. The song was recorded in Studios across California, alongside MXM Studios, based in Stockholm, Sweden. Inspired by Mariah Carey's first album, critics compared \"Birthday\" to the work of other musicians like Prince and Daft Punk. Through double entendres in the lyrics of \"Birthday\", Perry makes sexual references while celebrating a partner's birthday. Capitol Records sent the track to mainstream and rhythmic radio on April 21, 2014 as the album's fourth single.",
